                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 23-year-old female patient, admitted on 10/05/2025 with suspected tubal ectopic pregnancy following presentation with lower abdominal pain and vaginal spotting. On admission, a serum beta-hCG was markedly elevated, and transvaginal ultrasound confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture. Given the clinical findings and hemodynamic stability, the patient was counseled and consented for surgical intervention. She subsequently underwent laparoscopic salpingectomy with successful removal of the ectopic pregnancy. The postoperative course was uneventful. Wound care was provided and the patient was mobilized early. She was discharged home on 11/05/2025 in good general condition. Follow-up serum beta-hCG monitoring and outpatient gynecological review are recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
